// Adversarial: Burnout protocol activated via InjectProtocol, exercising the full
// RON-config → ShockwaveConfig wiring path under chaos input.
//
// The existing cascade_shockwave_stress scenario hardcodes ShockwaveConfig directly in
// initial_effects, giving false confidence: it does not exercise the path from
// ProtocolTuning::Burnout { shockwave_base_range, shockwave_range_per_level,
// shockwave_stacks, shockwave_speed } through activate() → BurnoutConfig insertion →
// burnout_on_bump → commands.fire_effect(ShockwaveConfig { ... }).
//
// This scenario activates Burnout through the real dispatch path so that:
//   1. BurnoutConfig is inserted with values from the loaded burnout.protocol.ron
//      (base_range=64.0, range_per_level=16.0, stacks=1, speed=200.0)
//   2. Chaos input at prob 0.8 forces high breaker movement, building heat rapidly
//      (fill_duration=4.0 at 64 Hz → full heat in ~256 frames), then mega-bumps fire
//      the shockwave via burnout_on_bump
//   3. The shockwave entity lifecycle (spawn → expand → despawn) is stressed under
//      sustained chaos across the full 8000-frame run
//
// Adversarial conditions:
//   - InjectProtocol at frame 10: protocol activates before physics warms up, testing
//     the lazy-insert BurnoutHeat path (first encounter inserts default, visible next tick)
//   - Chaos input (0.8): high movement ensures heat fills rapidly, maximising shockwave
//     spawns per run; also stresses breaker-edge positions during mega-bump timing
//   - Dense layout: maximises cells in shockwave radius so each shockwave triggers
//     the full HealDealt/DamageDealt pipeline, catching any NaN in range computation
//   - NoEntityLeaks: shockwave entities must despawn after expansion; any accumulation
//     indicates the shockwave lifecycle is broken under sustained bump pressure
//   - BurnoutHeatClamped: heat must stay in [0.0, 1.0] throughout; catches off-by-one
//     in burnout_update_heat fill/drain formula after the RON tuning sweep
//   - BoltInBounds: speed boost from burnout_tick_speed_boost must not bypass max clamp
//   - ExactlyOnePrimaryBolt: mega-bump + shockwave must not corrupt bolt entity count
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Dense",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.8)),
    max_frames: 8000,
    disallowed_failures: [BoltInBounds, BoltSpeedAccurate, BreakerCountReasonable, BreakerInBounds, BurnoutHeatClamped, ExactlyOnePrimaryBolt, NoEntityLeaks, NoNaN],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    seed: 1984,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "Burnout")),
    ],
)
